{"orgCode":"4440","name":"Department of State Hospitals","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"The Department of State Hospitals manages the nation's largest inpatient forensic mental health hospital system. Its mission is to provide evaluation and treatment for individuals with complex behavioral health needs in a safe, equitable, and responsible manner, by leading innovation and excellence across a continuum of care. The Department is responsible for the daily care and provision of mental health treatment of its patients. The Department oversees five state hospitals located in Atascadero, Coalinga, Metropolitan-Los Angeles, Napa, and Patton, with administrative offices in Sacramento and employs nearly 13,000 staff. In addition to the state hospital treatment, the Department provides services in contracted jail-based competency treatment, community-based restoration, community inpatient facilities and pre-trial felony mental health diversion programs, and the conditional release program.\n\nBecause the Department programs drive a need for infrastructure investment, the Department has a capital outlay program to support this need. For the specifics on the Department's capital outlay program see \"Infrastructure Overview.\"","totals":{"amounts":{"py":2800283,"cy":2936766,"by":2974960},"positions":{"py":10141.4,"cy":13214.4,"by":13255.3},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":152457,"cy":166364,"by":194624},"nongovernmental":{"py":1886,"cy":39973,"by":58093}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/4440","kind":"department","name":"Department of State Hospitals","code":"4440","amounts":{"py":2800283,"cy":2936766,"by":2974960},"positions":{"py":10141.4,"cy":13214.4,"by":13255.3},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":2800283,"cy":2936666,"by":2974860},"federal":{"py":0,"cy":100,"by":100}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4400","kind":"program","name":"Administration","code":"4400","amounts":{"py":259379,"cy":292442,"by":309390},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":259379,"cy":292442,"by":309390}},"description":"4400 - ADMINISTRATION\n\nDepartment of State Hospitals Headquarters oversees the California state hospital system, which provides mental health services to patients admitted into Department of State Hospitals facilities. Program Administration includes headquarters functions such as: policy development and management, program oversight, patients' rights coordination, clinical oversight, data research, fiscal, personnel and contracts management, as well as legal services.\n\nHospital Administration includes centralized functions and services that directly affect patient care but are administered centrally from headquarters.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":259455,"cy":292692,"by":314863}}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4400010","kind":"subprogram","name":"Headquarters Administration","code":"4400010","amounts":{"py":83622,"cy":108434,"by":113959},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":83622,"cy":108434,"by":113959}},"positions":{"py":319.7,"cy":383.7,"by":357.3},"description":"4400010 - HEADQUARTERS ADMINISTRATION\n\nDepartment of State Hospitals Headquarters oversees the California state hospital system, which provides mental health services to patients admitted into its system of care. Headquarters Administration includes functions such as: policy development and management, healthcare standards compliance, statewide patients' rights coordination, clinical oversight, data research, fiscal, personnel and contracts management, as well as legal services.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":83622,"cy":108634,"by":119280}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4400010/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":83622,"cy":108434,"by":113959},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":83622,"cy":108434,"by":113959}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":83622,"cy":108434,"by":113959}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4400010/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":200,"by":5321},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":200,"by":5321}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":200,"by":5321}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":200,"by":5321}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4400020","kind":"subprogram","name":"Hospital Administration","code":"4400020","amounts":{"py":175757,"cy":184008,"by":195431},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":175757,"cy":184008,"by":195431}},"positions":{"py":349.5,"cy":341,"by":341},"description":"4400020 - HOSPITAL ADMINISTRATION\n\nDepartment of State Hospitals Headquarters includes a Hospital Administration component. Hospital Administration includes centralized functions and services that directly affect patient care in DSH hospitals but are administered centrally from headquarters such as: technology services, hospital police and fire oversight, patient referral management, clinical recruitment, patient benefit and billing management, and Medicare revenue collection.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":175833,"cy":184058,"by":195583}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4400020/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":175757,"cy":184008,"by":195431},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":175757,"cy":184008,"by":195431}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":175757,"cy":184008,"by":195431}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4400020/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":76,"cy":50,"by":152},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":76,"cy":50,"by":152}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":76,"cy":50,"by":152}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":76,"cy":50,"by":152}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":76,"cy":250,"by":5473}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410","kind":"program","name":"State Hospitals","code":"4410","amounts":{"py":1975548,"cy":2000096,"by":2000198},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1975548,"cy":1999996,"by":2000098},"federal":{"py":0,"cy":100,"by":100}},"description":"4410 - STATE HOSPITALS\n\nThe state hospital system includes five state hospitals located at Atascadero, Coalinga, Metropolitan-Los Angeles, Napa, and Patton. Mental health treatment services at all facilities are delivered by clinical teams who provide full-time inpatient care to those with serious mental illness and are predominantly ordered for treatment by a criminal or civil court or by the Board of Parole Hearings (BPH). To a lesser extent, the Department of State Hospitals also receives referrals for state hospital treatment from county behavioral health departments or the public guardians, as well as from the California Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation (CDCR). The state hospitals treat the following types of patients: civil commitments under the Lanterman-Petris-Short Act (LPS); forensic commitments such as Incompetent to Stand Trial (IST), Not Guilty by Reason of Insanity (NGI), Sexually Violent Predators (SVP), and Offender with a Mental Health Disorder (OMD); and prisoners with mental illness (Coleman) from CDCR.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2127952,"cy":2166231,"by":2189370}}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410010","kind":"subprogram","name":"Atascadero","code":"4410010","amounts":{"py":349563,"cy":386083,"by":386401},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":349563,"cy":386063,"by":386381},"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"positions":{"py":1627.2,"cy":2205.6,"by":2212.1},"description":"4410010 - ATASCADERO\n\nThe Department of State Hospitals-Atascadero opened in 1954 and is located on the Central Coast of California in Atascadero (San Luis Obispo County). The hospital is a self-contained psychiatric hospital constructed within a security perimeter. The majority of the all-male patient population is remanded for treatment by Superior Courts or by BPH or CDCR pursuant to various sections of the California Penal Code and the Welfare and Institutions Code.\n\nDSH-Atascadero primarily serves the following four patient types: OMD, Coleman patients from CDCR, IST, and NGI.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":354482,"cy":392973,"by":394172}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410010/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":349563,"cy":386063,"by":386381},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":349563,"cy":386063,"by":386381}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":349563,"cy":386063,"by":386381}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410010/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410010/f0814","kind":"fund","name":"California State Lottery Education Fund","code":"0814","amounts":{"py":1,"cy":8,"by":8},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":1,"cy":8,"by":8}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1,"cy":8,"by":8}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410010/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":4918,"cy":6882,"by":7763},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":4918,"cy":6882,"by":7763}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":4918,"cy":6882,"by":7763}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":4918,"cy":6882,"by":7763},"nongovernmental":{"py":1,"cy":8,"by":8}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410020","kind":"subprogram","name":"Coalinga","code":"4410020","amounts":{"py":454009,"cy":455891,"by":457960},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":454009,"cy":455871,"by":457940},"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"positions":{"py":1785.5,"cy":2486.4,"by":2495.1},"description":"4410020 - COALINGA\n\nThe Department of State Hospitals-Coalinga opened in 2005 and is located on the western edge of Fresno County. The hospital is California's newest forensic mental health hospital and was created to primarily treat SVPs. It is a self-contained psychiatric hospital constructed with a security perimeter. CDCR provides perimeter security as well as transportation of patients to outside medical services and court proceedings. The majority of the all-male patient population is remanded for treatment by Superior Courts, BPH, or CDCR pursuant to various sections of the California Penal Code and the Welfare and Institutions Code.\n\nDSH-Coalinga primarily serves SVP, OMD and Coleman patients from CDCR.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":455990,"cy":456178,"by":458551}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410020/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":454009,"cy":455871,"by":457940},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":454009,"cy":455871,"by":457940}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":454009,"cy":455871,"by":457940}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410020/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410020/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":1981,"cy":287,"by":591},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":1981,"cy":287,"by":591}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1981,"cy":287,"by":591}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":1981,"cy":287,"by":591}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410030","kind":"subprogram","name":"Metropolitan","code":"4410030","amounts":{"py":294663,"cy":274517,"by":278240},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":294663,"cy":274497,"by":278220},"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"positions":{"py":1763.5,"cy":2335.6,"by":2351.2},"description":"4410030 - METROPOLITAN\n\nThe Department of State Hospitals-Metropolitan opened in 1916 and is located in Norwalk (Los Angeles County). The hospital is an open style campus with a security perimeter. Due to concerns raised by the community, DSH-Metropolitan maintains a formal agreement with the City of Norwalk and the Los Angeles County Sheriff not to accept patients charged with murder or a sex crime, or that are at high risk for escape.\n\nDSH-Metropolitan primarily serves the following four patient types: LPS, IST, OMD, and NGI.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":358268,"cy":348216,"by":357974}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410030/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":294663,"cy":274497,"by":278220},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":294663,"cy":274497,"by":278220}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":294663,"cy":274497,"by":278220}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410030/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410030/f0814","kind":"fund","name":"California State Lottery Education Fund","code":"0814","amounts":{"py":4,"cy":6,"by":6},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":4,"cy":6,"by":6}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":4,"cy":6,"by":6}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410030/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":63601,"cy":73693,"by":79728},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":63601,"cy":73693,"by":79728}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":63601,"cy":73693,"by":79728}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":63601,"cy":73693,"by":79728},"nongovernmental":{"py":4,"cy":6,"by":6}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410040","kind":"subprogram","name":"Napa","code":"4410040","amounts":{"py":419275,"cy":423887,"by":422150},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":419275,"cy":423867,"by":422130},"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"positions":{"py":1852.2,"cy":2683.4,"by":2704.2},"description":"4410040 - NAPA\n\nThe Department of State Hospitals-Napa opened in 1875 and is located in Napa County. The hospital was the first of the five State Hospitals and is the oldest California state hospital still in operation. It has an open style campus with a security perimeter.\n\nDSH-Napa primarily serves the following four patient types: LPS, IST, OMD, and NGI.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":466150,"cy":467339,"by":475516}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410040/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":419275,"cy":423867,"by":422130},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":419275,"cy":423867,"by":422130}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":419275,"cy":423867,"by":422130}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410040/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410040/f0814","kind":"fund","name":"California State Lottery Education Fund","code":"0814","amounts":{"py":10,"cy":4,"by":4},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":10,"cy":4,"by":4}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":10,"cy":4,"by":4}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410040/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":46865,"cy":43448,"by":53362},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":46865,"cy":43448,"by":53362}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":46865,"cy":43448,"by":53362}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":46865,"cy":43448,"by":53362},"nongovernmental":{"py":10,"cy":4,"by":4}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410050","kind":"subprogram","name":"Patton","code":"4410050","amounts":{"py":458038,"cy":459718,"by":455447},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":458038,"cy":459698,"by":455427},"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"positions":{"py":2285.2,"cy":2610.2,"by":2623.9},"description":"4410050 - PATTON\n\nThe Department of State Hospitals-Patton opened in 1893 and is located in San Bernardino County. The hospital has an open style campus with a security perimeter. CDCR correctional officers provide perimeter security and transportation at DSH-Patton as well as transportation of patients to outside medical services and some court proceedings.\n\nDSH-Patton primarily serves the following five patient types: LPS, IST, OMD, NGI and female Coleman patients from CDCR.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":493062,"cy":501525,"by":503157}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410050/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":458038,"cy":459698,"by":455427},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":458038,"cy":459698,"by":455427}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":458038,"cy":459698,"by":455427}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410050/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":20,"by":20}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410050/f0814","kind":"fund","name":"California State Lottery Education Fund","code":"0814","amounts":{"py":8,"cy":3,"by":3},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":8,"cy":3,"by":3}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":8,"cy":3,"by":3}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4410050/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":35016,"cy":41804,"by":47707},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":35016,"cy":41804,"by":47707}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":35016,"cy":41804,"by":47707}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":35016,"cy":41804,"by":47707},"nongovernmental":{"py":8,"cy":3,"by":3}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":152381,"cy":166114,"by":189151},"nongovernmental":{"py":23,"cy":21,"by":21}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4420","kind":"program","name":"Conditional Release Program","code":"4420","amounts":{"py":83504,"cy":93078,"by":99847},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":83504,"cy":93078,"by":99847}},"description":"4420 - CONDITIONAL RELEASE PROGRAM\n\nThe Conditional Release Program is the statewide system of community-based services for specified forensic patients. Mandated as a state responsibility by the Governor's Mental Health Initiative of 1984, the program began operations on January 1, 1986.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":83504,"cy":93078,"by":99847}}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4420010","kind":"subprogram","name":"Conditional Release Program","code":"4420010","amounts":{"py":69585,"cy":77965,"by":84288},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":69585,"cy":77965,"by":84288}},"positions":{"py":39,"cy":31.2,"by":23.2},"description":"4420010 - CONDITIONAL RELEASE PROGRAM\n\nThe Conditional Release Program General/Non-Sexually Violent Predators is comprised of NGI, OMD, and IST. Individuals suitable for this program may be recommended by the state hospital medical director to the courts for outpatient treatment. Currently, DSH contracts with county-operated and private organizations serving all 58 counties in the state with non-SVP commitments.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":69585,"cy":77965,"by":84288}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4420010/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":69585,"cy":77965,"by":84288},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":69585,"cy":77965,"by":84288}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":69585,"cy":77965,"by":84288}}}}]},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4420020","kind":"subprogram","name":"Conditional Release Program - Sexually Violent Predators","code":"4420020","amounts":{"py":13919,"cy":15113,"by":15559},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":13919,"cy":15113,"by":15559}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":15,"by":17},"description":"4420020 - CONDITIONAL RELEASE PROGRAM - SEXUALLY VIOLENT PREDATORS\n\nThe Conditional Release Program-Sexually Violent Predators was added to the Conditional Release Program effective January 1, 1996 per Welfare and Institutions Code 6604. Prior to the conditional release of the first SVP in 2003, conditional release providers did not have treatment services that would allow them to accept sexually violent predators as patients, requiring the Department of State Hospitals to enter into an annual contract with a single private provider serving 58 counties. Current statute requires SVPs be conditionally released to their county of domicile and sufficient funding be available to provide treatment and supervision services when an SVP is conditionally released into the community by court order.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":13919,"cy":15113,"by":15559}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4420020/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":13919,"cy":15113,"by":15559},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":13919,"cy":15113,"by":15559}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":13919,"cy":15113,"by":15559}}}}]}]},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430","kind":"program","name":"Contracted Patient Services","code":"4430","amounts":{"py":446013,"cy":447201,"by":529551},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":446013,"cy":447201,"by":529551}},"description":"4430 - CONTRACTED PATIENT SERVICES\n\nThe Department of State Hospitals contracts with local entities to provide mental health services to some of its patients outside of state hospital facilities. This includes the Admissions, Evaluation, and Stabilization Centers, Jail-Based Competency Treatment programs, IST Diversion programs, Community-Based Restoration programs and Community Inpatient Facility programs.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":446013,"cy":447201,"by":529551}}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430030","kind":"subprogram","name":"Other Contracted Services","code":"4430030","amounts":{"py":94749,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":94749,"cy":0,"by":0}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"4430030 - OTHER CONTRACTED SERVICES\n\nThe Other Contracted Services includes additional contracts with local entities to provide mental health services to some of its patients outside of state hospital facilities. Programs include IST Diversion and Community-Based Restoration programs.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":94749,"cy":0,"by":0}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430030/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":94749,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":94749,"cy":0,"by":0}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":94749,"cy":0,"by":0}}}}]},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430040","kind":"subprogram","name":"Other Contracted Services","code":"4430040","amounts":{"py":1358,"cy":938,"by":939},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1358,"cy":938,"by":939}},"positions":{"py":4,"cy":4,"by":4},"description":"4430040 - The Other Contracted Services focuses on policy development, program management and oversight of Jail Based Treatment Programs and Community Based IST Programs.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1358,"cy":938,"by":939}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430040/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":1358,"cy":938,"by":939},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1358,"cy":938,"by":939}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1358,"cy":938,"by":939}}}}]},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430050","kind":"subprogram","name":"Jail Based Treatment Programs","code":"4430050","amounts":{"py":138285,"cy":194075,"by":221022},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":138285,"cy":194075,"by":221022}},"positions":{"py":20.4,"cy":19.5,"by":19.5},"description":"4430050 - The Jail Based Treatment Programs focus on defendants deemed IST on felony charges and provides mental health treatment to these individuals in county jails, restoring them to competency, and allowing for participation in court proceedings.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":138285,"cy":194075,"by":221022}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430050/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":138285,"cy":194075,"by":221022},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":138285,"cy":194075,"by":221022}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":138285,"cy":194075,"by":221022}}}}]},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430060","kind":"subprogram","name":"Community Based IST Programs","code":"4430060","amounts":{"py":211621,"cy":252188,"by":307590},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":211621,"cy":252188,"by":307590}},"positions":{"py":19.7,"cy":31,"by":31},"description":"4430060 - The Community Based Incompetent to Stand Trial programs are partnerships with various counties to treat felony IST in a community mental health treatment setting. This includes Community-Based Restoration, Diversion and Community Inpatient Facilities.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":211621,"cy":252188,"by":307590}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4430060/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":211621,"cy":252188,"by":307590},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":211621,"cy":252188,"by":307590}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":211621,"cy":252188,"by":307590}}}}]}]},{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4450","kind":"program","name":"Evaluation and Forensic Services","code":"4450","amounts":{"py":29332,"cy":44939,"by":34217},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":29332,"cy":44939,"by":34217}},"description":"4450 - Evaluation and Forensic Services is comprised of the Offender with a Mental Health Disorder and the Sex Offender Commitment Programs as well as the Incompetent to Stand Trial Re-Evaluation Services program.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":29332,"cy":44939,"by":34217}}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4450010","kind":"subprogram","name":"Offender with a Mental Disorder and Sex Offender Commitment Program Evaluation Services","code":"4450010","amounts":{"py":20408,"cy":17224,"by":22779},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":20408,"cy":17224,"by":22779}},"positions":{"py":58.3,"cy":50.3,"by":50.3},"description":"4450010 - The Department is required to provide forensic evaluation services to determine if an inmate within the California Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation, prior to parole, requires continued treatment in a state hospital as an Offender with a Mental Health Disorder or as a Sexually Violent Predator as a condition of parole. The Department administers these services through the Offender with a Mental Health Disorder Program and the Sex Offender Commitment Program.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":20408,"cy":17224,"by":22779}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4440/4450010/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":20408,"cy":17224,"by":22779},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":20408,"cy":17224,"by":22779}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"Sta